    x++;
    printf("%d\n", x);
}

int main() {
    my_function(); // prints 1
    my_function(); // prints 2
    return 0;
}
```
In this example, the static variable `x` is initialized to 0 when the program starts. Each time `my_function()` is called, `x` is incremented by 1, and the new value is printed.

